$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of
(Z)-5-((3-aryl-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)thiazolidine-2,4-diones
(3a–h) A mixture of 1,3-diphenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-carboxaldehyde (1a, 1g, 4
mmol) and thiazolidine-2,4-dione (2, 0.51 g, 5 mmol) in ethanol (20 ml)
and 2–3 drops of piperidine, was refluxed. A solid separated out of the
reaction mixture within 15–20 min and the refluxing was continued for 5–6
h to complete the reaction. The reaction mixture was cooled to room
temperature, filtered and washed with ethanol to give the pure product.
(Z)-5-((3-(4-nitrophenyl)-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)thiazolidine-2,4-dione
(3g), 83% IR cm-1 (KBr): 1748 (C=O, thiazolidinedione ring), 1690 (C=O,
thiazolidinedione ring), 1574, 1512, 1450, 1342 and 1227; 1H NMR δ (300
MHz, DMSO-d6): 12.8–12.7 (bs, 1H, NH, exch. D2O), 8.537 (s, 1H,
Pyrazolyl-H), 8.412–8.386 (m, 2H), 7.977–7.929 (m, 4H), 7.671–7.284 (m,
4H); 13C NMR δ (75 MHz, DMSO-d6): 167.89, 167.66, 152.68, 139.25, 134.41,
130.91, 130.22, 129.62, 128.58, 128.12, 123.25, 122.12, 119.98 and
116.25; Anal. Found: C, 58.0; H, 2.98; N, 14.20. C19H12N4O4S (392.39)
requires C, 58.16; H, 2.84; N, 14.28%. Mp = 299–301 °C.
