$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Microwave-assisted Knovenagel Condensation of aromatic aldehydes with
malonic acid using alum-Cs2CO3. A mixture of aldehyde (1 mmol), malonic
acid (1 mmol), alum-Cs2CO3 (0.5 g), and distilled water (5 ml) in a 10 ml
CEM-reaction tube was sealed by rubber stopper and subjected to microwave
irradiation for 5 min at 100 °C in the commercial microwave reactor.
After that, the tube was cooled, and the completion of reaction was
checked by TLC. The reaction mixture was diluted with ethylacetate, and
alum-Cs2CO3 was filtered off. The organic layer was separated and dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4. The product was obtained after removal of the
solvent under reduced pressure and recrystallized from ethanol. The
catalyst was washed with distilled water (20 ml) and followed by ethyl
acetate (15 ml) and dried 1 h at 100 °C for further use. The structures
of the products were confirmed by IR, 1H NMR, mass spectral data, and
comparison with authentic samples. Product (Ar): 3a (C6H5). M.p:
136-137°C; Lit m.p: 135-136 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (450W), solid-supported catalyst, stereoselective,
alum-supported cesium carbonate used as catalyst, Knoevenagel
condensation, recyclable catalyst, sealed tube used, alternative reaction
conditions shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Syntheses of arylcinnamic acids, using Alum-Cs2CO3 as precursors of new
2-heterostyrylbenzimidazoles and their antimicrobial evaluation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ashok Kumar, T.; Kishore Babu, P. N.; Rama Devi, B.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Medicinal Chemistry Research (2015), 24(3), 1351-1364

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME259 STEP1
