$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of DNA-based barbiturates. As shown
in Scheme 1, a solution of the corresponding DNA-bases (for e.g., adenine
1 mmol) and formic acid (4 mmol) in distilled water, as a green solvent,
was allowed to reflux at 60°C over a period of 2-3 h. Then, it was cooled
down until the reaction mixture becomes a clear solution. The completion
of reaction was confirmed by TLC. In situ barbiturates were added again
and refluxed further for 3-4 h. As the reaction proceeds, the solid
products were separated out in the form of suspension and the
precipitated DNA-based barbiturates were separated by filtration, washed
with water three times followed by n-hexane, and then dried in a
desiccator.
5-(((2-Hydroxypyrimidin-4-yl)amino)methylene)pyrimidine-2,4,6-(1H,3H,5H)-trione
(BC), Yellow powder, Yield 82%. m.p.>250°C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO), 4.06
δ ppm (1H, dd, exocycyclic NH of purine ring, j = 15.68 Hz), 6.98 δ ppm
(2H, s, -CH of cytosine ring), 8.11 δ ppm (1H, dd, exocycyclic CH of
pyrimidine ring, j = 23.60 Hz), 8.16 δ ppm (1H, dd, NH of cytosine ring),
11.18 δ ppm (1H, s, NH of pyrimidine ring), 11.26 δ ppm (1H, s, NH of
pyrimidine ring). 13C NMR (400 MHz, DMSO), 78.53(C-7), 113.26 (C-9),
113.68 (C-8), 121.29 (C- 13), 126.43(C-12, C-14), 129.58 (C-11, C-15),
133.18 (C- 10) 157.53 (C-7), 161.35 (C-4, C-6), 169.34 (C-2) δ ppm. FTIR
(KBr) νmax cm-1: 1209 (m, -O-C stretching), 1354 (s, C-NH, aromatic
amine), 1632 (s, ═C-NH aliphatic amine), 1694 (s, C═O aromatic and
a,b-unsaturated ketone), 3072(m, CH-NH streching). λ max: 286.34 nm; (€:
1.14 × 105 L mol-1 cm-1 ); M.W. 249.18, ESIMS: m/z 251.14 (M + 2); Anal.
Calcd. for C9H7N5O4 (%):C 43.38, H 2.83, N 28.11. Found (%): C 43.40, H
2.79, N 28.12. IC50: WI-38: 97±0.13 μM; VERO: 90±0.12 μM; MCF-7: 60±1.32
μM; HEPG-2: 56±0.21 μM.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, Knoevenagel reaction
