$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of 2-styrylbenzimidazoles 6(a-x)
from 2-methylbenzimidazole 5(a-c). An intimate mixture of 5(a-c) (1.32 g,
10 mmol), aromatic aldehyde 1(a-h) (10 mmol) and boric acid (10 mol%) was
dissolved in 10 ml of glycerol in a 250-ml round bottom flask and allowed
to boil at 160-180 °C for 5-6 h. At the end of this period, the reaction
mixture was poured into ice cold water (25 ml). The reaction mixture was
diluted with ethylacetate, and the organic layer was separated, dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4. The product was obtained after removal of the
solvent under reduced pressure and recrystallized from ethanol. 6 (a-x).
The structures of the products were confirmed by IR, 1H NMR, mass
spectral data, and comparison with authentic samples. S. no.: 16.
Product: 6p; Yield: 80%. M.P: >250 °C; Lit. M.P: 287-291°C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, green chemistry-solvent, stereoselective, alternative
preparation shown
