$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Knoevenagel Condensation
in FBS.-The aldehyde (10 mmol) or ketone (10 mmol) was slowly added into
a mixture of Yb(OPf)3 (50 mg, 0.03 mmol), toluene (2 mL) and
perfluorodecalin (C10F18, cis and trans-mixture, 2 mL) containing the
active methylene compound (10 mmol). The mixture was stirred at 80°C for
the time indicated in Table 2. The bottom fluorous layer was then
separated (to be reused). The upper organic phase was washed with water
(10 mL), 10% NaHCO3 solution (10 mL) and water (10 mL x 2), and dried
over MgSO4. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure and the
residue was purified by a silica gel column chromatography (40% EtOAc in
petroleum ether) or by recrystallization from ethanol to give the
Knoevenagel product. Entry: 20; yield: 80%. Mp or bp (mm Hg): 185-188
(15) [lit.19 185-188 (15)]°C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-process simplification, Knoevenagel condensation,
fluorous biphasic system used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ytterbium perfluorooctanesulfonate-catalyzed Knoevenagel condensation in
a fluorous biphasic system
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yi, Wen-Bin; Yin, Ya-Qing; Cai, Chun
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Preparations and Procedures International (2006), 39(1), 71-75

