$DATUM 534-17-8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A typical procedure for the Knovenagel
Condensation of aromatic aldehydes with malonic acid using alum-Cs2CO3.
To a mixture of aldehyde (1 mmolol), malonic acid (1 mmolol), and
distilled water (10 ml) in a round-bottom flask (50 ml), alum-Cs2CO3 (0.5
g) was added. The reaction mixture was allowed to heat on water bath at
100 °C for appropriate time (Table 1) with shaking regularly. The
completion of the reaction was monitored by TLC. The reaction mixture was
diluted with ethyl acetate, and alum-Cs2CO3 was filtered off. The organic
layer was separated and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The product was
obtained after removal of the solvent under reduced pressure and
recrystallized from ethanol. The catalyst was washed with distilled water
(20 ml) and followed by ethyl acetate (15 ml) and dried for 1 h at 100 °C
for further use. The structures of the products were confirmed by IR, 1H
NMR, mass spectral data, and comparison with authentic samples. S. no.:
6. Product : 3f ; Yield: 80%. M.p: 242-244 °C; Lit m.p: 243°C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported catalyst, stereoselective, alum-supported cesium
carbonate used as catalyst, Knoevenagel condensation, alternative
reaction conditions shown, recyclable catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Syntheses of arylcinnamic acids, using Alum-Cs2CO3 as precursors of new
2-heterostyrylbenzimidazoles and their antimicrobial evaluation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ashok Kumar, T.; Kishore Babu, P. N.; Rama Devi, B.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Medicinal Chemistry Research (2015), 24(3), 1351-1364

